msgstr ""

#: src/admin/pages/dashboard/pages/no-login.js:82
msgid ""
"When does the content of the \"Select Page For Non-Logged-in Visitor\" "
"appear?"
msgstr ""

#: src/admin/pages/dashboard/pages/no-login.js:90
msgid ""
"If a user navigates directly to the frontend dashboard without logging in, "
"the content of the chosen page on the \"Select Page For Non-Logged-In "
"Visitor\" section will be displayed for them."
msgstr ""

#: src/admin/pages/dashboard/pages/sidebar.js:217
msgid "What is sidebar content?"
msgstr ""

#: src/admin/pages/dashboard/pages/sidebar.js:222
msgid ""
"Sidebar content is prominently displayed at the side of the Frontend "
"dashboard, serving as a focal point for your dashboard's visual "
"presentation. You have the flexibility to incorporate all available "
"elements into the sidebar content, giving you the ability to enable, "
"disable, and seamlessly sort these elements according to your preferences. "
"This feature empowers you to create a personalized and visually engaging "
"dashboard sidebar tailored to your specific needs."
msgstr ""

#: src/admin/pages/dashboard/pages/sidebar.js:234
msgid ""
"The separation element serves as the focal point from which other elements "
"diverge, creating a distinct visual separation to the top and bottom. "
"Rather than acting as a center element, it functions as the origin of the "
"layout, determining the arrangement of elements for an organized and "
"visually appealing Frontend dashboard."
msgstr ""

